        "title": "Water Pump Leak / Coolant Loss on 3.6L V6",
        "description": "The 3.6L V6 in the Enclave is known for water pump failure, attributed in part to dissimilar metals in the pump that expand and contract at different rates and eventually allow coolant to seep. Owners frequently find coolant puddling after the car is parked and may see overheating if the leak is severe. It is considered a fairly routine wear item on this engine.",
